00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.887
Okay guys, so take a
look at this scene from

00:08:27.887 --> 00:08:29.280
"The Great Gatsby."

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:31.150
I didn't even really like
this movie very much,

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:34.230
but this is one scene that
I remember as clear as day,

00:08:34.230 --> 00:08:36.120
and I watched this like three years ago.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:39.920
This is the scene where Spider
Man meets Leonardo DiCaprio.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:41.150
I forget the characters' names.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:43.730
Look at the way this interaction goes.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:44.563
- You see...

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:49.143
I'm Gatsby.

00:08:50.208 --> 00:08:51.744
- Oh, you're...

00:08:51.744 --> 00:08:54.244
(grand music)

00:08:56.190 --> 00:08:58.880
His smile was one of those rare smiles

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.740
that you may come across
four or five times in life.

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:05.360
It seemed to understand
you and believe in you,

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:09.090
just as you would like to be
understood and believed in.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:11.500
- Sorry, old sport, I thought you knew.

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:15.000
- Please just, I don't know
what to say. Please forgive me.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:15.920
- It's quite all right.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.820
- [Nick] I've had so much to drink.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:19.820
- Mr. Gatsby, sir, Chicago (indistinct).

00:09:21.144 --> 00:09:22.780
- I'll be just a minute.

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:25.595
I'm taking my new hydroplane
out in the morning.

00:09:25.595 --> 00:09:28.176
Would you like to go with me?

00:09:28.176 --> 00:09:29.530
- What time?

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:30.510
- A time that suits you.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:32.360
- When he meets Gatsby for the first time,

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:36.010
he feels like there is
understanding behind his smile.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.920
As powerful as Gatsby is,

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:40.860
he still took the time to
put his hand on his shoulder,

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:44.100
look him in the eye,
and really pay attention

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:47.130
and focus on what Peter Parker was saying.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.520
So the last tip is focus.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.040
Pretend that the person in front of you

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:53.490
is the only person in the entire world.

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.970
And this channel is all about focus.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:58.240
The skill of focus translates well

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.710
to human interaction as well.

00:09:59.710 --> 00:10:01.930
If you learn to minimize your cell phone

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:03.410
and social media use,

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.910
if you learn to focus
on slower pace things

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.590
and really honing in on
things you find boring,

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.330
even boring conversations,

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:12.480
then you'll be able to
make people feel valued

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.770
and appreciated and listened to.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:16.090
That's all that people want.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:18.910
Even when they go on long
spiels about all their goals

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:21.627
and ambitions, all they want to hear is

00:10:21.627 --> 00:10:23.440
"That is incredible."

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:24.810
You know? "Good for you."

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:27.970
So why not make somebody's day by actually

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:29.840
even pretending that you care?

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:31.200
Sometimes that's all people need.

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:34.170
They just need somebody who
pretends like they care.

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.560
Bonus points if you
actually learn to care.

00:10:36.560 --> 00:10:39.270
So guys, these are just some
of the lessons I learned

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:41.180
from "How to Win Friends
and Influence People"

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:42.210
by Dale Carnegie.

